# Check out LF everywhere, Windows included (git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true).
# A CRLF checkout breaks the POSIX shim bin/anywhere ("#!/bin/sh\r"), which Claude Code runs
# through Git Bash on Windows, and the SKILL.md frontmatter. PowerShell reads LF scripts fine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe needs CRLF: LF-only batch files can mis-parse labels and goto targets.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
